Z||000000||Topknot||05-14-2001||12:30 PM||||Hallo all,<P>Ok, I am still in the process of going thur the Forums past posting on Clutch topics, so I am trying BUT...<P>I just spent 3 hours bleeding the dang thing and after replacing both the Master and Slave I am able to select gears but to my sadness the Gears don't seem to "catch".  <P>Now I can't select the gears without pushing in the Clutch so I know that my cylinders are working to an extent.  But now, am I looking at having to drop the whole cradle to get to the clutch to remove and replace or is there something I'm missing that I've not thought of yet.<P>I have manuels and have spent two nights reading web sites and this excellent forums topics but still not seeing the light of my problem.  I bought a 1986 1/2 GT V6, the engines in great condititon.  It's clean in the engine compartment.<P>But the car did sit for a few years in a gentlemens garage, (He was the only owner) and I did find I had to get things lubed and moving again to function.  <P>So any pointers or suggestions for problem solving would be most happyly welcomed!!<P>Topknot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>P.S. After going thru quite a few postings about Clutchs I did a few checks and here is some updated info.<P>1 - The Magnet Sticks to the Clutch Pedal so it must be the Steel one and not the Alumium<P>2 - My Slave Cylinder doesn't have any type of "bracket" meaning that the thing bolts directly to the engine supports supplied.  Now It's a GT V6 5 Speed..Do I need a bracket..?<P>3 - Fluids are totally new and bleed to the max.  I cant shift unless I push the clutch in but then when I release it feels like it's trying to catch but not totally getting there.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Topknot (edited 05-14-2001).]||||reg||5
